2026-09-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2262) 'make it with the pen and wear it together
 # uuid: 1ccb9b31-4e0b-5d11-8d1e-9b4183abc0ca
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l3
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-09-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Pen meshing in a shared world with graded annotations: a person draws their character and outfit with the meshing pen, wears it and moves in it where others see it, and gets a grade that teaches them to draw better
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2262) 'transport-meshing-pen, the stage guests it builds, and the V-Sekai client and server that host the loop
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2262) 'A person draws an outfit with the meshing pen, wears it, and moves in it where others see it.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2262) 'An anonymous 16-person survey of the shared world's own community asked for two things: to create and share what others can see (8), and to be with people (8).
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Each release is read through its own gate.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2262) 'make it with the pen and wear it together
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2262) 'The strategy is a release ladder: each release is a whole product put in front of real people to test one assumption, never a half-built release.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2262) '- RFD66606-2234 (dress-on pipeline), the loop the releases ride on.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2262) '- RFD66606-1053 (OpenUSD as the internal format).
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2262) '- RFD66606-2229 (interchangeable parts), the rule new parts answer to.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2262) '- RFD66606-2267 (persona NPCs in ported scenes), a parked content idea behind the releases, not one of them.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2262) 'The loop
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2262) 'The loop is godot-sandbox guest ELFs a host loads, with no engine module of its own. The scoring it relies on runs the same shape: EditScore and MaskScore are decision models, godot-sandbox guests on ggml-rd and compute-rd, not a second runtime. OpenUSD is the internal format, VRM the one a player shares.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2262) 'The releases
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2262) 'One release advances at a time. Later releases change with what the active one teaches. Each release names what it tests, who tries it and where it stands.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2262) '- **Demand test.** Do people want to make 3D things with a pen in VR, and what do they make? The public tried the published CASSIE sketch study (Yu et al., doi 10.1145/3411764.3445158). Done: people liked it, and wearables exist in what they drew (36 study shoes, a dress, two hats).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2262) '- **First testable release.** Can a person draw an outfit, wear it, and show it to someone who talks with them? The simulator first, a replayed sketch (RFD66606-2263); then the first rung, two people in one zone with the garment made on a worker zone (RFD66606-2287). Active.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2262) '- **Shareable release.** Will people save, share and wear what they made where others see it? The same creators and whoever they share with, phones included. Next: save as OpenUSD, export VRM, wear it and move in it in the world.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2262) '- **First usable release.** Will creators use it for their own avatar? Early adopters from the survey. Later: their own body (ANNY fitted in a guest, or their own mesh), rigged, delivered as VRM.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2262) '- **First lovable release.** Will people show it to friends? Anyone. Later: the character in parts (body, head, hair), and more emotes and dances.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2262) '- **Full product.** Only if people ask for it. Later: faces and hair motion; nobody in the survey asked.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Enabling work (CI, the drape's precision, comfort settings against motion sickness, the org's rules) is not a release. It runs as the active release needs it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Where it runs
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2262) 'The first host is &{repo("transport-meshing-pen")}: the xr-grid pen with the stage guest ELFs it builds inserted through godot-sandbox. It has two implementations, chosen per process through the OpenXR runtime manifest (`XR_RUNTIME_JSON`):
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2262) '- the simulator, OXRSys with a replayed hand, repeatable on a desk and in CI;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2262) '- a standalone VR headset on a Linux-based OS, a person holding the pen.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Later hosts are the shared world's client and a dedicated server running the same ELFs, for people on phones and anyone who would rather not wait; the server hands back the VRM.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Formats
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2262) '- OpenUSD is internal: Pixal3D's answer, the loop's meshes and materials, and a person's strokes (one linear `BasisCurves` prim per stroke, the boundary mark a per-curve primvar).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2262) '- VRM is delivery: what a player loads and shares.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2262) 'The grade that teaches
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2262) 'The loop ends in a critique, not only a wearable. The score step returns a grade with annotations on the drawing, so a person reads where it marked them down and learns to draw better; the wearable and the lesson come from one pass.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2262) 'The grader is a decision model, EditScore retrained, and it runs inside the loop, so it is sized to the loop. A checkpoint that needs a workstation to answer is too large; the target is a compact retrain that answers in the sandbox, not the biggest model available.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Measured 2026-09-27: stock EditScore (Qwen3-VL-8B with its LoRA) does not judge segmentation masks. On 23 social-VR frames it agreed with a MoGe-3 depth-edge check on 6. A readout of the score-slot logits, with no reasoning generated and the frame prefix shared, answers about 12x faster than generating the reasoning but ranks only 0.42 to 0.52 (Spearman) against it. Both point to the compact retrain, not the stock model.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Shared means moving
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Shared means the person locomotes: they walk, turn and sit in the world wearing what they drew, and others see the outfit move with them. The shared world's client animates locomotion by sliding the avatar in its T-pose, and that is not acceptable: nothing bends, drapes or plants a foot, so a wearable seen there is seen standing still.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Shared also means voice: people talk to each other while they move, over voice chat from the `modules/speech` module on entities-godot's `feat/module-speech` branch.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2262) 'The loop's locomotion is its own: a generated clip retargeted onto the avatar (&{repo("interactor-motion-guest")}; gate 10 stays in the archived `interactor-dress-on`), with the body grounded on the GPU as one rigid move per frame, so a foot stays where it lands and a seat holds a sitting body. Every contact is held to a penny (1.52 mm), within 100 ms end to end and 1.0 ms of GPU time per frame on the standalone headset.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Moving in it: the mocap track, parked
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Wearing it and moving together needs body motion to drive the avatar. That track is Sinew, inertial motion capture from a worn suit. It sits behind the releases above, recorded here so it is not lost and not scheduled.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2262) '- Shelved 2026-09-26: the mount-drift calibrator's training corpus shipped as `chibifire/mount-drift-caldata-motion` (558 rows of continuous microduck-gated clips, human and starforged phenotypes). Training the calibrator on it and measuring arm and hand mount recovery against a real-caldata baseline remains. Unpark when GPU budget and a held-out real capture are both in hand.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2262) '- Shelved 2026-09-26: the IMU-recovery half, raw sensor to per-tracker orientation, stays unproven. Unpark with a clean low-IK recapture, the worn suit with motion smoothing and IK off, so the vendor pose approximates the raw tracker orientations for a direct match.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2262) '- Shelved 2026-09-26: motion generation runs on the owned GPUs now (CUDA in WSL, both cards, via the bf16 op_repeat fix in the shared ggml). Unpark to scale the corpus with continuous motion-matching sequences when training needs more than the pilot.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2262) '- Shelved 2026-09-26: fleet agents mint GitHub tokens from the bao GitHub secrets engine and land PRs through the merge queue. Unpark to make that the standing path when multi-agent coordination is the card in motion.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Faces: the track behind the full product, deferred
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2262) 'Faces belong to the full product, which waits on people asking. The work toward them is recorded here so it is not lost and not scheduled.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2262) '- Shelved 2026-09-27: avatar-person segmentation for faces. RF-DETR seg-nano runs on ggml-rd as a godot-sandbox guest (`interactor-rfdetr-seg-guest`; gate 9, in the archived `interactor-dress-on`, passes against a CPU flat control and a `GGML_RD_FAULT` negative control). A fine-tune loop exists (interactor-rf-detr-ggml PR #25), and a 300-image CC0 VRM pilot carries exact masks (datasource-anny-render-corpus PR #41). Unpark when a release needs avatar-person detection.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2262) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2262  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2262) 'One asked for emotes; none for rendered clips, hair motion or faces.
 # tags: rfd:details
